1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,760
Hi everyone, I'm Gareth. I love hacking and finding creative ways to solve problems and

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:16,040
explore systems. When I'm not hacking, I'm building tools to hack faster and smarter.

3
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:22,280
One of my favourite projects is Hackverter, a Burpsuite extension I created to handle

4
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:26,320
all kinds of conversions and make life easier for hackers like me.

5
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:33,880
Recently, I got really excited to hear that we're adding AI functionality to the Montoya API in Burp.

6
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:40,720
It's a game changer that makes adding AI features to BAPS easier than ever. Let me show you some of

7
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:47,280
the new features I added to Hackverter. Before we start using these enhancements, we first need to

8
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:54,380
configure Burp and Hackverter to enable the AI features. So head over to the extensions tab.

9
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:03,000
And check the use AI checkbox. Then go to the Hackverter menu.

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,320
And click settings. Then check all the AI features and enable them.

11
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:21,020
You also want to allow code execution tags in order to do some of the demos in the video.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:30,580
And hit update. Great, we're all set. So now we'll demo some of the new AI features.

13
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:36,560
For the first demo, I'm going to show you how to create AI custom tags.

14
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:41,520
Hackverter supports different programming languages such as Python and JavaScript.

15
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:45,440
But now you can use AI prompts to perform conversions.

16
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,000
Imagine you have an MD5 hash that you want to crack.

17
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:56,540
And because the AI has traversed the whole web, it knows the plain text of many MD5 hashes.

18
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:03,160
So this is an MD5 hash of let me in.

19
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:07,720
So let's use AI custom tags to crack it.

20
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:14,300
First, go to the Hackverter menu bar and click create custom tag.

21
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,720
Then we've got the custom tag window.

22
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:29,240
In the custom tag window, I'm going to type a name crack MD5 as the tag name.

23
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:32,100
Then I'm going to enter a prompt.

24
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:38,460
Crack this MD5 hash.

25
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:40,480
Cool.

26
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,020
So click create tag.

27
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:47,780
And now this tag is available in the custom section.

28
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,620
And here you can see crack MD5.

29
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:51,800
So let's click that.

30
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:57,040
And then this sends the information off to the AI.

31
00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:00,440
The AI uses the prompt and cracks the hash.

32
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,720
Dead easy.

33
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:13,560
In this second demo, I'm going to show you how easy it is to create custom tags even without programming knowledge.

34
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:18,020
Let's open the create new custom tag window again.

35
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:25,640
Now enter reverse me as the tag name.

36
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,220
Reverse me.

37
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:31,320
And select JavaScript as the language.

38
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:36,760
In the code box, let's enter your prompt.

39
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:42,100
So in this case, reverse this text.

40
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,780
And click use AI to generate code.

41
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,400
Now Hackverter will ask you for some input.

42
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,600
So let's give it some input.

43
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,720
A, B, C.

44
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:55,540
And the expected output is C, B, A.

45
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:56,820
Great.

46
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:57,540
Press OK.

47
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:04,040
And it's created a custom tag for you automatically just from your inputs.

48
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:12,980
The advantage over this than using an AI tag is that once the code is created, you don't use any more tokens.

49
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,420
So it's really handy.

50
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:17,620
So let's finish off and create that tag.

51
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:28,160
In this demo, I'm going to show you how the AI automatically created a description of the custom tag we created.

52
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:34,540
First, let's navigate to the custom tag we previously created by clicking the Hackverter menu.

53
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:39,300
And click list custom tags.

54
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:44,020
And select the reverse me tag that we created.

55
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:45,180
And click edit.

56
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:53,980
As you can see, the AI has automatically created a text description of what the code does.

57
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:58,160
This is useful if you're not familiar with the programming language in question.

58
